{"abstract":"In this paper, we discuss an ethnographic field study conducted with a single 8-person development team operating within an established indie game company located in Copenhagen, Denmark, to explore how members of a development team – in this case mainly programmers and designers – coordinate their design ideas and development processes. In a view that accepts “the heterogeneity of production logics within the games industry” (Kerr 2017,76), our study of a single company in Denmark contributes new insights on organized and managed team creativity by adding to this pool of varying forms of development. The paper inquires and develops a perspective to analyse collaborative game-making within a studio workplace. We explore two formats of game development team meetings, Sprint Reviews and Sprint Retrospectives, to understand the ways in which teams work together to balance ‘creative-rational tensions’ (Tschang 2007) between given expectations and deadlines as well as personal expressive interests.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Poulsen, Mark Staun","Wirman, Hanna Elina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759422"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Case study","Collaboration","Ethnography","Game Development","Game design","game design praxeology","game production studies","studio studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"creative rational tensions in game development a danish case study on team collaboration","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.26503/todigra.v7i1.2184","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759422","ids":["itu-d5be4233-417c-4a58-b563-a86176d4169c"],"keyword":["case study","collaboration","ethnography","game design","game design praxeology","game development","game production studies","studio studies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-0E413FDB4A6CA8E9D506E50E8ABD6A8E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.26503/todigra.v7i1.2184","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Games Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark Staun","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"6826c79c-8024-4f3c-bebf-f07d51e8988b","name":"Poulsen, Mark Staun","orcid":"0009-0006-6649-8165","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanna Elina","key":"wirmanpau","last":"Wirman","locid":"9ba013db-4c4d-41dd-be12-dbe188f67f29","name":"Wirman, Hanna Elina","orcid":"0000-0002-9578-2708","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.26503/todigra.v7i1.2184","issue":"1","journal":"ToDiGRA","pages":"89-124","status":"p","title":"ToDiGRA","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d5be4233-417c-4a58-b563-a86176d4169c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Creative-Rational Tensions in Game Development : A Danish Case Study on Team Collaboration","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759422","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This PhD research project (Autumn 2024– Spring 2027) explores interdisciplinary game development from within game development teams in Denmark. It will consist of three qualitative case studies in Danish game studios and education through which I apply ethnographic participation to develop grounded and context dependent results. Overall, I undertake research across game design praxeology, organizational science, and sociology of work to analyse the working and learning environment of game makers in its socio-economic context: How are interdisciplinary work forms and competences cultivated among newcomers for working in the Danish game industry? The primary objective, then, is to examine how newcomers to the Danish game industry are trained for interdisciplinary work and contextualize such expertise from within studio workplaces and Danish society. Like any case study, my project will provide rich contextual descriptions of challenges that newcomers face, and inform debates on game education curriculum and policy in Denmark","author_count":4,"contributors":["Poulsen, Mark Staun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776429"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI PLAY","title":"Annual Symposium on Computer-Human Interaction in Play"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Case study","Ethnography","Game Development","Game design","Interdisciplinary collaboration","Situated learning","game production studies","studio studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"interdisciplinary game development situating the professional expertise and skill building among danish game workers","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3665463","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776429","identifier":[{"id":"85211624780","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9d350d1c-aa91-42ac-9e0a-4b2aa56eb460"],"keyword":["Game development","case study","ethnography","game design","game production studies","interdisciplinary collaboration","situated learning","studio studies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-724CD5CFAF1CA702B19C683B7C810254"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3665463","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark Staun","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"6826c79c-8024-4f3c-bebf-f07d51e8988b","name":"Poulsen, Mark Staun","orcid":"0009-0006-6649-8165","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Oğuz ‘Oz’","key":"burukpedh","last":"Buruk","name":"Buruk, Oğuz ‘Oz’","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Guo","key":"freemanpedh","last":"Freeman","name":"Freeman, Guo","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Juho","key":"hamaripedh","last":"Hamari","name":"Hamari, Juho","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3665463","eisbn":["9798400706929"],"pages":"438","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Companion Proceedings of the 2024 Annual Symposium on Computer-Human Interaction in Play","title":"CHI PLAY Companion '24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85211624780"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9d350d1c-aa91-42ac-9e0a-4b2aa56eb460"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Interdisciplinary Game Development : Situating the Professional Expertise and Skill-Building among Danish Game Workers","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776429","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
